I never thought I was going to be an  entrepreneur growing up I didn't have  entrepreneur role models nobody in my  family was an entrepreneur nobody in my  extended family was an entrepreneur I  went to school with people who all  wanted to have jobs you know make it in  the corporate world my teachers all  pushed me towards that path to I never  thought I was going to be an  entrepreneur so I pull up my yearbook at  the end of the year all of the graduates  opens my high school graduates we all  had to answer some questions and some of  them are pretty funny when we flip the  page 5 here so i was asked things i'd  like to forget about my high school  experience and i wrote all of my science  courses what famous quote you wish you  had said to yourself I wrote if you want  to get the fruit you have to go out on a  limb still like that one and the last  one was where do you see yourself 20  years from now let me bring this up  where do you see yourself 20 years from  now vice president of a major investment  bank that was always my dream I wanted  to be an investment banker that's what i  thought was what i wanted to do because  i wasn't exposed to the world of  entrepreneurship it all changed in  university and university i met up with  two people who had a business that  wasn't doing well they asked me to join  as an owner and help them grow this  thing up and i thought you know what you  want the fruit you got to go to a limb  let's try something new and I went for  them and I loved it and and you know  what it wasn't working out at the start  I was making three hundred dollars a  month and struggling that's you know  below the poverty line and an  interesting thing happened in my last  year I got opportunities to work with  merrill lynch and Mackenzie strategic  consulting Merrill Lynch is one of the  top investment banks in the world and  mackynzie was a company that I always  looked up to and admired and so here it  is that this is this is my dream job  right in front of me what I always what  I said in my high school year but this  is what I wanted to have happen and  they're flying me to New York and  they're putting me up in expensive  hotels and they're schmoozing mean  wanted me to join their business and  something just felt off  because i love doing my company and even  though I was only making three hundred  dollars a month I felt like I would  regret it if I didn't go and do that my  own business instead of working for  another company and it was hard and I  struggled with it and I worried that I  would I just made the biggest mistake of  my life and my friends and family  thought it was crazy how could you take  this three hundred dollar-a-month job  instead of going for this eighty to a  hundred thousand dollar a year job right  how could I do that doesn't make sense  is what I always wanted my life and then  you know what I'm so glad I'm so glad  now that I made that decision I had the  you know courage somehow the trust my  gut but I wonder what if I'd never met  those people in University what if I'd  never joined that business I'd be off  doing this thing that is not meant for  me because I never knew if  entrepreneurship was meant for me I  never had a test I never had a guy i  never had that exposure growing up and  so I wanted to help people who are going  through the same thing and I created  Zuba 000 which is the Entrepreneurship  mindset test to help you figure out if  entrepreneurship is is for you or not  you know the help expose you to that  world and what it is is a hundred  questions you go through it and it it  basically by the end of it you figure  out are you supposed to be an  entrepreneur right now or not and you'll  either get a clear indication you know  yes you might get a no and that's okay  that gives you some confidence to you  know to know that it's not for you and  anywhere in between and the in between  is important too because it it'll tell  you where the holes are and you're  thinking it'll tell you where you're  going to fall down in the future it'll  tell you why you're going to be holding  yourself back it'll tell you the people  who you need to surround yourself with  to accomplish your goals they'll tell  you where your fears are going to be and  what you need to overcome to get to  become that successful entrepreneur that  you're after I wish I wish I had this  when I was in high school so I wouldn't  make that mistake I wish I had this when  I was trying to make that decision  between being an entrepreneur  her and working at what I thought was my  dream job this is meant for people who  are struggling to find out is  entrepreneurship really for you if  you're in that zone this is going to  help you on top of the hundred questions  it also shares my story how I got  started it shares stories some famous  entrepreneurs like Larry Ellison and  Jeff Bezos and Martha Stewart and George  Lucas and how they got started and their  challenges and what their advice is to  find out of entrepreneurship is for you  and how to get started I hope you'll  check it out again I wish I had this  when I was going through those problems  and I know it's going to help a lot of  people out so you can check it out in  the link below enjoy it and believe
 

